-  "THE_CORPUS_EACH_FIGURE_IS_OVER": "NAMED, because it moved during the session. The 408-of-539 and 327-occasion figures are over the archive AS IT STOOD BEFORE LEG 3 LANDED. Re-running the producer after leg 3 gives 337 occasions and 71.3322%, 95% Wilson [67.5644%, 74.8254%], because leg 3's own mathematical-guard blocks joined the corpus. Neither figure is wrong; a proportion over a growing archive has no fixed value, and the project has already recorded that 'a typed figure over a growing corpus is not merely unverifiable; it is guaranteed to go stale'. The producer reproduces whichever is asked for, and the DIRECTION is unchanged: between 2 and 3 of every 4 refusals were an attempt to reach the code path.",
-  "evidence_line": "Over 220 archived classifier logs and 2,273 override lines: of 539 mathematical-guard blocks, 408 had a CODE destination -- 75.6957%, 95% Wilson [71.9011%, 79.1267%] -- across 327 distinct (run, finding, move) occasions, 104 finding identifiers and 32 runs. Producer: scripts/the_code_path_guard_is_off_in_non_software_2026-10-15.py",
-  "his_words": "Verdict, yes, fix it.",
-  "options": [
-   "RULE YES on the one-clause narrowing: `math_guard = (regex is MATHEMATICAL and not llm_primary and llm_type not in _code_types)` (recommended). It extends to every domain the behaviour software already has, and the named dominated property is whether a code claim can reach the only cell that can ground it.",
-   "RULE NO and keep the maths label absolute outside software. The cost is that 327 measured occasions of a proposed rescue stay refused, and Haiku stays unable to make its most valuable move in exactly the domains you asked about.",
-   "RULE a CONFIDENCE TEST instead: allow the move to a code type only above a stated confidence, rather than unconditionally. 0 of the 327 occasions fell below 0.65, so a 0.70 threshold would admit nearly all of them."
-  ],
-  "ruled": "2026-10-16",
-  "title": "Haiku cannot rescue a misrouted code bug outside the software domain",
-  "what": "You asked whether restricting Haiku to code-based issues risks making it redundant in non-code STEM experiments, and asked for a fix. The measured answer corrects the premise and then finds a real defect running the OTHER way. Haiku holds 3 live roles and only 1 is domain-gated at all: the classifier. The dedup assessor and the Ouroboros librarian reader run in every domain. Even the gated one is DEMOTED outside software, not switched off -- it still made 22 classifications in a mathematics run. But `math_guard` blocks ANY move away from a `mathematical` label outside software at ANY confidence, including the move TO a code type, which is the one destination that CAN ground a code claim. So the rescue the classifier exists to perform is reachable in software only.",
-  "what_the_ruling_means": "FIX. Narrow the mathematical guard so the move to a code type is permitted outside software.",
-  "what_was_already_fixed": "The mirror-image hole WAS fixed tonight and needed no ruling because it only ADDS protection: the code-path guard was wired to the software domain, so outside software a true code claim could be demoted OFF the code path. Measured: 10 distinct findings of 333 SEMI-ACTIVE overrides, 3.0030%, 95% Wilson [1.6392%, 5.4387%], 8 of them from exp38 -- the experiment the guard's own comment cites as its motivation. Now domain-independent, 51 tests green, and 2 mutations turn them red (16 failures and 3 failures)."
- },
- "defect:proven-floor-used-as-a-ceiling-in-the-decomposition-decision": {
-  "MEASURED_2026_10_15_AND_IT_REFUTES_PART_OF_THE_ORIGINAL_CLAIM": {
-   "A_SECOND_SELF_CORRECTION": "An intermediate hypothesis that the live runner only READS the key and never writes it was also wrong. An AST scan for assignment sites finds 2 writes in reference_runner_v3.py, at lines 11418 and 11461, where it takes max(existing, prompt_chars). The hypothesis came from grepping only the first few hundred lines and would have produced a confident wrong diagnosis; the AST check caught it.",
-   "WHAT_ACTUALLY_REMAINS_AND_IT_IS_WORSE_IN_ONE_RESPECT": [
-    "4 of the 5 PAID seats carry EXACTLY 465,206 -- CC2, ChatGPT, Codex and Gemini, identical to the character. DeepSeek alone differs at 110,076. An identical figure across 4 vendors of different architectures is not a per-seat observation.",
-    "It has not moved in 185 days, since 2026-04-13, across 26 revisions of the file. The mundane reason is that no paid seat has been dispatched in that window, which is the standing no-paid-dispatch directive working as intended -- NOT a write bug.",
-    "It is now structurally un-correctable. DECOMPOSE_HARD_FLOOR_CHARS is 80,000 and every payload above it is force-decomposed, so no single dispatch can exceed 80,000 chars. The derived ceiling from 465,206 is 0.9 x 465,206 = 418,685, far above the floor, so for a paid seat the size-based futility guard can effectively never fire and the 465,206 can never be re-exercised or corrected downward by ordinary running.",
-    "This is the figure already implicated in a measured quality collapse. The code's own comment records Exp 39-0: 'their fingerprints reported 465K observed capacity x 0.9 safety margin = 418K >= 369K, no decompose, quality crashed' on 369K dispatches to CC2, ChatGPT and Gemini."
-   ],
-   "WHAT_REFUTED_IT": "The ratchet DOES climb wherever dispatches actually happen. Measured from git history of the fingerprint files across every revision: CC2-SIM's observed maximum rose 3 times -- 35,013 on 2026-08-30, 63,136 on 2026-08-31, 74,140 on 2026-09-08, 80,517 on 2026-10-04 -- monotone non-decreasing with 0 falls, cross-checked by NumPy (minimum successive difference 0) and SymPy (monotonicity over the exact integers).",
-   "producer": "measured inline from `git show <sha>:bench/fingerprints/*.json` across every revision; figures reproduced in this entry and in the session note.",
-   "the_claim_as_recorded": "A seat's proven capacity is used as a ceiling, so its observed maximum can never rise -- 'a ratchet that cannot climb'."
