-  "recommendation_standards": "ADDITIVE: option 1 removes nothing and enables nothing; the actuator stays in record-only mode, which is the state the project's own additive standard prefers for a mechanism whose effects are not yet measured. SIMPLEST SUFFICIENT: it produces the only evidence the unattended cycle actually lacks, a record of what the loop WOULD do, without the irreversible half. COMPOSABILITY: options 1 and 2 do not compose, they are sequential: 2 is only decidable once 1 has produced a record, so no composed fix is claimed. 1 CAVEAT ON THE RECOMMENDATION ITSELF: option 1's first clause, making the pause reachable, is a BUILD, and his deferral governs builds here, quoted in this entry as \"It should be built and tested at the appropriate time\". So option 1 splits into a build he has deferred and a mode that is already the default. Nothing in it is urgent.",
