 **B78. ~~A seat now says what it is missing before a run discovers it, which is the backend half of the model-and-keys surface he asked for.~~** **[COMPLETED 2026-11-06 - DONE/COMMITTED]** Added 2026-11-02T14:54:52+00:00. **STATUS: BUILT, TESTED, COMMITTED. Not a decision.** **HIS ASK, 2026-11-02, verbatim:** *"researchers should be able to search for/add models trivially from a search box in the UX, enter all their API keys, and logins for OpenRouter, and for the various model vendors they might have access to, and from any local models they have on their machines. They shouldn't need to think, or concern themselves with the underlying mechanics of how this works in reality. Which is what I mean by making the process trivial."* And on doing it: *"This may require you to make some adjustments to the existing UX work as required. But there is no reason why you shouldn't do it."* **WHY THIS ENTRY EXISTS AT ALL: B20's closing paragraph names this as authorised work that reached NO entry.** His ticket of 2026-10-20 reads *"I am not asking you to build the UX now. [...] you can build the UX backend, so that the eventual UX can map cleanly on to it"*, and that ticket was MERGED into B20 on `task_ref` alone without checking the subject matched, so the UX backend existed as authorised work in exactly 1 place in the project -- a merged ticket. **WHAT WAS ACTUALLY MISSING, AND IT IS NOT A SEARCH BOX.** A seat needs 2 independent things and the project had no surface showing either: a ROUTE, meaning a `ModelConfig` carrying `api` and `model_id` plus whatever credential that route needs; and CALIBRATION, meaning an entry in each of the 5 per-model tables. **The Fable seat had the route and was missing 4 of the 5 calibration entries, and that gap was found by a run FAILING rather than by anything asking.** `bench/seat_readiness.py` is the asking, reached through a new `seats()` function in `bench/ux_backend_2026-10-20.py`, which was 311 lines with no notion of a model, a key or