 **B95. ~~A mutation harness whose anchor stops matching SKIPS the mutation, still prints "N of N applied" and still exits 0, so a lost property reads as a complete run.~~** **[COMPLETED 2026-11-06 - DONE/COMMITTED]** Added 2026-11-03T01:29:53+00:00. **STATUS: FIXED IN 4 HARNESSES, TESTED, AND IT FOUND 3 LIVE LOSSES. Not a decision.** **FOUND BY IT HAPPENING TO ME, 2026-11-03, 10 minutes after I caused it.** Hoisting the fix comparator's key set to a module constant -- the B93-adjacent repair that made its refusal message name all 5 required keys instead of 4 -- rewrote the text that `scripts/the_fix_comparator_mutations_2026-11-02.py` anchors 1 of its mutations on. The harness printed `[SKIP] the declared direction requirement is removed from BOTH checks`, then printed **`11 of 11 applied mutation(s) turned the suite RED`** and **exited 0**. The direction requirement was unguarded by mutation and every summary line said the run was complete. **THE ARITHMETIC IS WHY, AND IT IS THE PIN-A-SET-NOT-A-COUNT SHAPE AGAIN.** The exit test was `red == applied and applied`. A skipped mutation lowers `applied` AND is absent from `red`, so the equality still holds: the skip moves BOTH sides of `red == applied` and cancels itself. Comparing 2 totals passes; only comparing the MEMBERSHIP of the declared mutation list tells the truth. **★ THE 2 FIGURES IN THIS SENTENCE WERE WRONG AND ARE CORRECTED IN PLACE, 2026-11-03, by re-verifying this entry's own commit. It read *of 14 harnesses that can skip an unapplied anchor, 4 gated their exit on `applied`*. The measured values are 12 and 5.** **THE 4 WAS WRONG BECAUSE THE CLASSIFIER READ THE PRINTED MESSAGE RATHER THAN THE EXIT CONDITION** -- it grepped `applied mutation(s) turned` instead of `red == applied and applied`, so `scripts/the_two_directive_repairs_mutations_2026-11-02.py`, which words its output differently and carries the identical fault, was filed as safe. That is `execute-do-not-grep` inverted: reading what the code says about itself instead of what it decides, and the 5th instrument of the night to answer a narrower question than the one it was asked. It is now fixed, so all 5 gate on the declared total. **THE 14 WAS WRONG IN THE FLATTERING DIRECTION, which is the one that deserved the most care:** the scan accepted any file mentioning `SKIP` anywhere, including in prose, rather than the `[SKIP` the harnesses actually print, and the strict predicate gives 12 of 15 files. An inflated denominator made the problem look more widespread than it is. **THE DEFECT AND THE REPAIR ARE UNCHANGED BY EITHER CORRECTION.** The sentence as originally written follows, for the record: of 12 harnesses that can skip an unapplied anchor, 5 gated their exit on `applied` rather than on the DECLARED total** -- `the_cy_gate_mutations_2026-11-02.py`, `the_declaration_admission_mutations_2026-11-02.py`, `the_fix_comparator_mutations_2026-11-02.py` and `the_round_clock_mutations_2026-11-02.py`. The other 10 already record a NOT APPLIED entry as a FAILURE and so cannot hide one. **THE FIX IS 1 LINE EACH: the denominator is now `len(MUTATIONS)`, the number DECLARED, which a skip cannot move.** **AND IT IMMEDIATELY FOUND 3 LIVE LOSSES IN 2 OF THE 4, each of which had been exiting 0.** `the_cy_gate_mutations` was silently skipping *the refusal no longer names Monitor, the channel that works*. `the_declaration_admission_mutations` was silently skipping 2: *the composer key map is no longer filled, the 1 entry that caused 3 absences* and *the fingerprint is no longer filled*. Those 3 properties are now LOUD -- both harnesses exit non-zero until their anchors are repaired -- which is the correct state for a lost guard and is the whole point of the change. **REPAIRING THOSE 3 ANCHORS IS FOLLOW-UP WORK AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT DONE HERE**, because each needs the current form of its own subject established first, and a harness that refuses is safe whereas one that passes falsely is not. **THE FIX CANNOT TURN THE BOARD RED, checked before committing rather than after:** no test executes a mutation harness, the pre-commit hook does not run them, and `bench/tests/test_todays_producers_are_reached_2026-11-02.py` lists all 4 under its NOT_RUN_HERE exclusion with the reason *invokes pytest; would recurse* -- its 38 tests pass unchanged. **WHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND 4 FILES:** every figure of the form *N of N mutations red* that this project has ever quoted rests on a denominator a skip can move. The 10 safe harnesses were safe by construction rather than by design, and nothing had compared the 2 shapes until now. **13 pre-existing ruff findings across those 4 files are left alone and flagged**, not fixed: 13 at HEAD and 13 after, none at a line this entry touches.
