-  "evidence_line": "A futility guard treats the symptom: when the unsplittable part already exceeds the limit, splitting is dominated on per-request bytes, total bytes and request count, proved by 3 tools agreeing.",
-  "his_words": "Fix it all.",
-  "options": [
-   "RULE: RESET the 4 paid seats' observed maximum to a per-seat figure before paid dispatch resumes (recommended). The shared 465,206 is not an observation of any one of them, and leaving it means the decomposition decision for every paid seat is driven by a number none of them produced.",
-   "RULE: RAISE or REMOVE the 80,000 hard floor so the figure can be re-exercised. This is the design decision the code's own comment names -- 'Changing it alters routing for paid seats and is a design decision, not a repair' -- and it reopens the Exp 39-0 quality-collapse risk the floor was added to prevent.",
-   "RULE: LEAVE BOTH and accept that paid decomposition routing rests on a 185-day-old shared constant. Honest, and it costs nothing until paid dispatch resumes.",
