-  "ruled": "2026-10-16",
-  "title": "The proven-floor ceiling: PARTLY FALSIFIED on measurement, and what remains is sharper",
-  "what": "The decomposition decision reads the largest prompt a seat has accepted and splits the job above 90% of it. The code's own words call that a proven floor, meaning the model has shown it can handle at least that much, and then treats it as a limit.",
-  "what_the_ruling_means": "FIX.",
-  "why": "With the specification delivered whole, the standing instructions are 74,177 characters, and all 6 simulated seats, 100.0000%, Wilson [60.9666%, 100.0000%], would have force-split every dispatch on the size of their own instructions, while no paid seat would have. A confound that fires only in the cheap runs is the worst shape there is."
