- "task:B20": {
-  "evidence_line": "Producers: scripts/has_the_bound_orchestrator_been_built_or_run_2026-11-02.py reporting 4 of 4 built, and scripts/the_unattended_loop_has_never_been_reachable_2026-11-04.py reporting 0 of 352 runs with the review flag set as at 2026-11-08, Wilson [0.000000, 0.010795], Clopper-Pearson [0.000000, 0.010425]; it read 0 of 351 with Wilson [0.000000, 0.010826] and Clopper-Pearson [0.000000, 0.010455] on 2026-11-04, all 3 of which reproduce exactly, so 1 further run has landed, the NUMERATOR held at 0, and the upper bound tightens rather than the claim changing, on 3 independent predicates. The declaration's own line references are now carried as data in a CITATIONS dict of 9 entries and checked by bench/tests/test_the_actuator_holds_its_contract_2026-11-03.py; 2 of the 4 pointing into the runner had drifted, by 23 and 7 lines, 0.500000, Wilson [0.150039, 0.849961] Option 1's central claim, that record-only mode produces the evidence the unattended cycle needs, was an ASSERTION until 2026-11-08 and is now MEASURED BY EXECUTION: scripts/are_the_two_switches_the_whole_set_2026-11-08.py drives the real loop through the actuator's own _runner seam across 5 cases at exit 0, and shows that with the review flag on and the act flag withheld the classifier still reaches RESUME and record() writes it to actuator_decisions.jsonl with all 9 evidence fields while re-invoking nothing. The same producer REFUTES a third gate: with both flags set the loop acts, 3 invocations and 2 resumes driven, and the 3 further conditions are not switches, the pulse being written by the watchdog, the launch command being a required argument, and --max-resumes defaulting to 3 read out of argparse rather than assumed. So the 2 switches are the whole set and they are INDEPENDENT, which is what makes option 1 a distinct setting rather than a weaker version of option 2.",
